  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Rod A and Rod B are made of the same material.</p>\n<p>The two ends of rod A are held at temperatures <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"20\\:{}^{\\circ}\\textup{C}\"></span>and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"100\\:{}^{\\circ}\\textup{C}\"></span>. Thermal energy is transferred through rod A at a constant rate <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The two ends of rod B are held at temperatures <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0\\:{}^{\\circ}\\textup{C}\"></span> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"160\\:{}^{\\circ}\\textup{C}\"></span>. </p>\n<p>Given that rod B has twice the length and half the cross-sectional area of rod A, what is the rate of thermal energy transfer through rod B?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4R\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2R\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{R}{4}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{R}{2}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
